### Test the Caldova Supply Autopilot over the Responses protocol
#
# Prereqs:
#   1. VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
#   2. azd auth login (or az login)
#   3. Fill in @endpoint from your deployment:
#        azd env get-values | Select-String AZURE_AI_PROJECT_ENDPOINT
#   4. Get a token and paste it into @token below:
#        az account get-access-token --resource https://ai.azure.com --query accessToken -o tsv
#
# Hosted agents can ONLY be called through the agent endpoint path used below —
# posting to {project}/openai/responses returns HTTP 400 telling you the correct path.

@endpoint = https://<your-account>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<your-project>
@agent = caldova-supply-autopilot
@apiVersion = 2025-11-15-preview
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Inspect the agent — shows BOTH protocols are registered
GET {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Foundry-Features: HostedAgents=V1Preview,AgentEndpoints=V1Preview

# Look for:
#   "protocols": [ "activity", "responses" ]
#   "authorization_schemes": [ { "type": "Entra" }, { "type": "BotServiceRbac" } ]


### 2. Web IQ — works under app identity ✅
POST {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}/endpoint/protocols/openai/responses?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Any weather or carrier disruptions this week that could affect cold-chain shipments?",
  "stream": false
}


### 3. Foundry IQ — works under app identity ✅
POST {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}/endpoint/protocols/openai/responses?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Is a major cold-chain excursion eligible for replacement and credit?",
  "stream": false
}


### 4. Work IQ — does NOT resolve here ❌ (needs user-delegated OBO, i.e. Teams)
POST {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}/endpoint/protocols/openai/responses?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Any urgent supply escalations in your mailbox?",
  "stream": false
}

# Expected: "I'm not able to directly access your mailbox in this chat."
# This is the demo beat — same agent, same code, different identity.


### 5. Streaming variant (set stream: true to watch SSE deltas)
POST {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}/endpoint/protocols/openai/responses?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Why was Summit Dose awarded CALD-201?",
  "stream": true
}
